{"step_index":65,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-07T05:47:47Z","content":"Git을 처음 설치하셔서 **커밋을 남기는 사람의 이름과 이메일 정보**가 등록되지 않아서 발생하는 에러입니다!\n\n제가 이 프로젝트 폴더(`mini-kingdom`)에 한해서 임시 이름과 이메일로 설정을 지정하고, 아까 실패했던 커밋을 마저 진행해 드리겠습니다.","thinking":"**Diagnosing the Error**\n\nI've zeroed in on the core of the problem. It seems the user's Git installation lacks author identification, manifesting as the \"Author identity unknown\" error. I'm focusing on the need for name and email configuration within the user's Git setup.\n\n\n**Devising the Approach**\n\nI've decided to address the Git configuration issue directly. My strategy involves using `git config` with the username for the user's name and email as default values locally. I'll test running these commands within the repository to resolve the \"Author identity unknown\" error, prioritizing an immediate fix for the user.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cd \"c:\\Users\\JCHJ\\Desktop\\Antigravity\\mini-kingdom\"\ngit config user.name \"JCHJ\"\ngit config user.email \"JCHJ@example.com\"\ngit commit -m \"Initial commit: 게임 기획 문서 및 코어 프레임워크 1차 구현\"","Cwd":"c:\\Users\\JCHJ\\Desktop\\Antigravity\\mini-kingdom","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Configuring Git and Committing","toolSummary":"Git Config & Commit"}}]}
