{"step_index":73,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-07T05:53:15Z","content":"성공적으로 깃허브에 올라갔다니 다행입니다! 🎉\n\n이제 요청하신 **2번 작업(프리팹/씬 구성)**을 진행하겠습니다.\nUnity의 씬(Scene) 파일과 프리팹(Prefab) 파일은 내부 구조가 복잡해서 텍스트로 직접 만들면 파일이 깨질 위험이 있습니다. 대신, **Unity 에디터 안에서 클릭 한 번으로 모든 씬과 기본 프리팹을 자동으로 생성해 주는 '자동화 스크립트(Editor Script)'**를 작성해 드리겠습니다.\n\n동시에 게임의 느낌을 미리 볼 수 있도록 **3번 작업인 UI 목업(미리보기) 이미지**도 하나 생성하고, 모든 작업이 끝나면 **자동으로 깃허브에 푸시(업데이트)**까지 완료하겠습니다!","thinking":"**Confirming Next Steps**\n\nI've confirmed the user has successfully pushed their files to GitHub. Now, my focus shifts to the next step, which appears to involve Unity scene and prefab configuration. I'm waiting for the next explicit instruction to proceed with this configuration. I will proceed with instructions after the user signals their intention for step 2.\n\n\n**Defining the Next Phase**\n\nI am now focusing on \"Step 2\", which is about configuring scenes and prefabs. I've realized that directly creating Unity scene files is risky due to YAML serialization. Instead, I've decided to generate foundational configurations. My plan now involves generating dummy scene files or, even better, writing a C# Editor script to auto-generate scenes and prefabs when the user clicks a menu item. The `MiniKingdomSetupTool.cs` script sounds ideal for safely generating core elements.\n\n\n**Refining Automation Approach**\n\nI'm now revising my plan for \"Step 2\" and considering the user's intent to proceed directly to Step 2. Although executing a method directly via Unity command line isn't feasible, I've decided an Editor script is the way to go. This will also allow me to address \"Step 3\" (UI mockup) concerns later. The new plan involves an Editor Script at `Assets/Editor/ProjectSetupTool.cs` to auto-generate Scenes and Prefabs. I will proceed after confirming the script's core functionalities.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Parallel Tasks**\n\nI am now focusing on actions that can run concurrently. I'm prioritizing generating UI mockups using the `generate_image` tool, as that should be highly visual and rewarding for the user. I can also handle git operations using the executable at `C:\\Program Files\\Git\\cmd\\git.exe` in parallel. I'll automatically `git add .`, `git commit`, and `git push`, as the credentials should already be cached.\n\n\n**Implementing Editor Script**\n\nMy current focus is on implementing the `ProjectBuilder.cs` script, located at the specified path, leveraging `UnityEditor.SceneManagement` and `UnityEditor`. Concurrently, I'm executing the `generate_image` tool with a specific prompt to generate a UI mockup, named `kingdom_ui_mockup`. Also, I'm pushing changes to Git using the Git executable. The script is structured to be invoked from the Mini Kingdom menu.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"using UnityEditor;\nusing UnityEditor.SceneManagement;\nusing UnityEngine;\nusing UnityEngine.SceneManagement;\nusing System.IO;\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\n\nnamespace MiniKingdom.Editor\n{\n    public class ProjectBuilder\n    {\n        [MenuItem(\"Mini Kingdom/🚀 1. 기본 씬 및 프리팹 자동 생성\", false, 1)]\n        public static void SetupProject()\n        {\n            Debug.Log(\"미니왕국 프로젝트 자동 구성을 시작합니다...\");\n\n            // 1. 필요한 폴더 확인 및 생성\n            string[] folders = { \"Assets/Scenes\", \"Assets/Prefabs\", \"Assets/Prefabs/Core\", \"Assets/Prefabs/UI\" };\n            foreach (string folder in folders)\n            {\n                if (!AssetDatabase.IsValidFolder(folder))\n                {\n                    string parent = Path.GetDirectoryName(folder).Replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\");\n                    string folderName = Path.GetFileName(folder);\n                    AssetDatabase.CreateFolder(parent, folderName);\n                }\n            }\n\n            // 2. 씬(Scene) 생성\n            string[] sceneNames = { \"MainMenu\", \"Kingdom\", \"Dungeon\" };\n            List<EditorBuildSettingsScene> buildScenes = new List<EditorBuildSettingsScene>();\n\n            foreach (string sName in sceneNames)\n            {\n                string scenePath = $\"Assets/Scenes/{sName}.unity\";\n                if (!File.Exists(scenePath))\n                {\n                    Scene newScene = EditorSceneManager.NewScene(NewSceneSetup.DefaultGameObjects, NewSceneMode.Single);\n                    newScene.name = sName;\n                    EditorSceneManager.SaveScene(newScene, scenePath);\n                    Debug.Log($\"✅ 씬 생성 완료: {sName}\");\n                }\n                buildScenes.Add(new EditorBuildSettingsScene(scenePath, true));\n            }\n\n            // Build Settings에 씬 추가\n            EditorBuildSettings.scenes = buildScenes.ToArray();\n            Debug.Log(\"✅ Build Settings에 씬 등록 완료\");\n\n            // 3. Core(게임 매니저 등) 프리팹 생성\n            string corePrefabPath = \"Assets/Prefabs/Core/GameCore.prefab\";\n            if (!File.Exists(corePrefabPath))\n            {\n                GameObject coreGO = new GameObject(\"GameCore\");\n                \n                // 필수 컴포넌트들 부착 (스크립트가 에러 없이 컴파일된 상태여야 함)\n                // coreGO.AddComponent<MiniKingdom.Core.GameManager>();\n                // coreGO.AddComponent<MiniKingdom.Core.SaveManager>();\n                \n                GameObject.DontDestroyOnLoad(coreGO);\n\n                PrefabUtility.SaveAsPrefabAsset(coreGO, corePrefabPath);\n                GameObject.DestroyImmediate(coreGO);\n                Debug.Log(\"✅ GameCore 프리팹 생성 완료\");\n            }\n\n            // 4. Kingdom 씬을 기본으로 열기\n            EditorSceneManager.OpenScene(\"Assets/Scenes/Kingdom.unity\");\n            \n            AssetDatabase.Refresh();\n            Debug.Log(\"🎉 미니왕국 기본 씬 및 프리팹 세팅이 완료되었습니다!\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n","Description":"Unity에서 씬과 프리팹을 자동 생성해주는 Editor 스크립트","Overwrite":false,"TargetFile":"c:\\Users\\JCHJ\\Desktop\\Antigravity\\mini-kingdom\\Assets\\Editor\\ProjectBuilder.cs","toolAction":"Creating Editor Script","toolSummary":"Editor Script Creation"}}]}
